The endpoint does not explicitly handle a missing user.

A clearer implementation is:

from fastapi import HTTPException

@app.get("/users/{user_id}")
def get_user(user_id: int):
    user = database.get(user_id)

    if user is None:
        raise HTTPException(
            status_code=404,
            detail="User not found"
        )

    return user

This gives the client an appropriate HTTP response instead of returning an ambiguous null result.

